<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indrapura (Champa)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Indrapura was a capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, at Đồng Dương in Quảng Nam province, from the late 9th century. Its great Buddhist monastery, founded by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indravarma">Indravarman</a> II in 875, was one of the largest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>. The Vietnamese ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh">Lê Hoàn</a> sacked Indrapura in 982, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> later moved their capital south to Vijaya.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indrapura-champa.jpg" alt="Indrapura (Champa)" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: [Tycho] talk , http://shansov.net · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Th%C3%A1p_%C4%90%E1%BB%93ng_D%C6%B0%C6%A1ng_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
